# Demolition Field: the searches do not depend on the land having been destroyed (ruling 2022-10-14). In response to the ability
# Bot2 animates Creeping Tar Pit and casts Revitalizing Repast on it (indestructible until end of turn); the target is still a
# legal target (a land an opponent controls), so the ability resolves, the destroy does nothing, and Bot2 may still search for
# a basic land (Forest), as may Bot1 (Plains).

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Island
Demolition Field
Island x16
Plains

[Bot2 Deck]
Creeping Tar Pit
Mox Jet
Mox Sapphire
Mox Emerald
Revitalizing Repast
Island x14
Island
Forest

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Creeping Tar Pit.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Demolition Field.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Demolition Field.Activate(Ability: Destroy; Bot2.Battlefield.Creeping Tar Pit)
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Creeping Tar Pit.Activate(Ability: Until end of turn)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Creeping Tar Pit.Activate(Ability: {T}: Add {U} or {B}; Color: Black)
Bot2.Hand.Revitalizing Repast.Cast(Creeping Tar Pit)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Accept
Bot2.Search(Forest)
Bot1.Accept
Bot1.Search(Plains)

[Expect]
Bot1.Graveyard = Demolition Field
Bot1.Battlefield = Island; Island; Plains
Bot2.Graveyard = Revitalizing Repast
Bot2.Battlefield.Creeping Tar Pit.Tapped = true
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Tapped = false
